A||||4||Homicidal||A few questions on shing my rims up, if you please???||||5||
Z||000000||Homicidal||06-20-2000||03:42 AM||||I attempted one rim today.  I cleaned it with Paint Thinner before hand, and then proceeded to the paint stripper (in gel form).<P>I liberally applied it, and the clearcoat came off easily on the main larger areas.  But along the groove closest to the tire and the groove closest to the main part of the rim, the clearcoat is still pretty apparent.<P>How do I go about getting it out of there?  Just keep appliying the stripper?  Are there any other more powerful chemicals I could use?<P>One more question:  what tool should I use to remove the clearcoat?  I used a wire brush and it started to scratch the surface of the rim.  Do I even need a tool, should it lift off easily?  <P>Any help is appreciated!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||06-20-2000||09:20 AM||||Try a toothbrush, or a nylon bristle parts cleaning brush.<BR>You might try a brass-bristle brush (say THAT three times, quickly) but go slow. I'm not sure which is harder, aluminum or brass. Might scratch, too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||06-20-2000||09:54 AM||||To get the "hard to reach" areas use a BRASS detail brush.(brass won't hurt/scratch the aluminum) As for the stubborn areas for paint and clearcoat use "Permetex Spray-on Gasket Remover". The gasket remover does a better job than the paint stripper stuff. Just spray on and let it sit about 15 minutes, then bursh away. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||06-20-2000||11:45 AM||||Thanks, Oreif. I couldn't remember if I used a brass brush on mine, or not. <BR>I keep hearing about the Permatex gasket remover. <BR>Did you have to reapply it?<BR>I used the "gel" stripper on my Formula wheels. Had to reapply 2-3 times, to get it all. Was *not* a lot of fun.||||reg||14
Z||000004||Oreif||06-20-2000||11:58 AM||||I had to re-apply the gasket remover only once. The small circular dimples between the lugnut holes on the GT rim and the small diamond areas just outside the lugnut area.<BR>I used a small wooden spatula to clean them out my brass brush was too big for these small areas.<BR>||||reg||1
